Block Builder (apps/blocks)

Game (engine/)
  ClassiCube 1.3.8, by UnknownShadow200 and the ClassiCube contributors: a
  custom Minecraft Classic compatible game written from scratch.
  License: BSD 3-Clause (engine/LICENSE.txt, which also has the licenses of
  the parts ClassiCube includes, such as Emscripten's).
  Source: https://github.com/ClassiCube/ClassiCube, commit
  33891a4e7e586941240261bc911312f228be57d3, with frunk.store's changes for
  the browser in engine/classicube-web.patch (also
  tools/blocks/classicube-web.patch in https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store,
  whose tools/build-blocks.mjs builds it).
  The changes: the page says where the texture pack and sounds are, whether
  to show the touch controls and how many canvas pixels make a CSS pixel;
  a world the page kept opens as a path, and a new one takes its size,
  land and seed from the page; web_save() saves the world for the page and
  web_escape() is its Menu button; a saved world remembers which way the
  player faced; a controller listed twice (raw and standard) is read once;
  no player skins are downloaded in single player; the frame rate isn't
  shown unless asked for; and no "unsaved changes" prompt on leaving, as
  the page saves the world itself.

Textures (data/textures.zip)
  The block, hotbar and player textures are from Mineclonia
  (https://codeberg.org/mineclonia/mineclonia, commit
  490f3c62e609e87f615703f4fe75b9ba7e05cfbc), whose textures are based on
  the Pixel Perfection resource pack by XSSheep and Pixel Perfection Legacy
  by Nova Wostra, with changes and additions by the Mineclonia and
  MineClone2 contributors (data/MINECLONIA-LEGAL.md).
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  frunk.store adapted them for this game with tools/blocks/pack.mjs: laid
  out in ClassiCube's terrain atlas, grass and leaves tinted green, some
  wool colours tinted from white wool, and the animated water, lava, fire
  and magma frames moved into animations.png. The adapted textures are
  shared under the same license.
  The buttons, crosshair, clouds and touch stick are drawn by
  tools/blocks/pack.mjs (frunk.store), under the same license.
  The font (default.png) is drawn from Monocraft by Idrees Hassan
  (https://github.com/IdreesInc/Monocraft, commit
  e498bf70aeb25b4bdcff1e44d878fb2cb4f7c2a9), under the SIL Open Font
  License 1.1 (data/MONOCRAFT-LICENSE.txt), by tools/blocks/font.mjs.

Sounds (data/sounds/)
  From Mineclonia's mcl_sounds, renamed to the sounds the game asks for.
  Their authors and licenses (CC BY 3.0, CC BY-SA 3.0, CC BY-SA 4.0, CC0
  and WTFPL) are listed in data/SOUNDS-CREDITS.txt.

